        answer: "No. TVA dams provide significant flood control storage, but they are designed for specific events and operating rules, and tributary streams can flood independently of the main river. FEMA floodplain maps still govern construction near the river and its creeks. Engineers design to the mapped base flood elevation regardless of dam operations upstream.",
