        body: "Compaction grouting is the least disruptive fix for voids and loose solution fill. Grout injected under controlled pressure compacts the surrounding soil and fills the void, with the grout takes telling the engineer how much emptiness was actually down there. Verification borings or probes after grouting confirm the treatment worked. For large or shallow features, open excavation and replacement with engineered fill, compacted and tested in lifts under observation, removes the doubt along with the bad ground.\n\nThe foundation choice follows the remediated ground. Drilled shafts socketed into sound rock below the karst zone are the standard for commercial buildings, because they do not depend on the treated soil performing perfectly. Lighter structures on well-remediated sites may use reinforced mat or stiffened slab foundations designed to span a future localized void. Either way, the drainage design protects the investment: lined stormwater conveyances, positive grading away from the building, and no infiltration practices over known karst features. The permit set documents the investigation, the remediation, and the verification so the plan reviewer can approve with confidence.",
